===== 4. the lifecycle, guard ON (section 3 as specified) =====
# ABI v1 section 3: the lifecycle
#   init-guard: ON -- every entry point checks (section 3 as specified)
#   build id:   ak-core 0.0.0 abi1 ak-core
#   ak_abi_version(): 1, the host was generated against 1

# Each case below is a FRESH PROCESS. `ak_init` is one-shot and there is no
# `ak_shutdown`, so a suite that ran two cases in one process would be
# measuring the second case against the first case's installs.

case                         exit   what it establishes
uninit-first                 ok     an entry point BEFORE ak_init
    guard ON: encode before ak_init -> Err(-10) (want Err(-10))
init-ok                      ok     ak_init returns AK_OK and ak_initialized() flips
    ak_init -> 0 (AK_OK=0), detail 0
    ak_initialized() -> 1
init-twice-same              ok     the same options again: AK_ALREADY_INITIALIZED, a SUCCESS
    first 0, second 1 (AK_ALREADY_INITIALIZED=1)
    # and it is a SUCCESS, not an error: a host library that initialises
    # defensively must not fail because another one got there first.
init-twice-differ            ok     different options: refused, AK_DETAIL_OPTS_DIFFER
    first 0, second -8, detail 2 (AK_DETAIL_OPTS_DIFFER=2)
    # The one-shot installs cannot be redone, which is also why there is
    # no ak_shutdown.
init-differ-collide          ok     R-D9: options built to collide under an XOR fold: still refused
    first 0, second -8, detail 2 (want -8, AK_DETAIL_OPTS_DIFFER=2)
init-bad-version             ok     a host generated against another ABI: AK_ERR_ABI
    ak_init(abi_version=8) -> -11, detail 1
    ak_initialized() -> 0 (must still be 0)
    # The check is made by the side that KNOWS what it was generated
    # against, once, at the only point where failing is cheap.
init-null                    ok     a null options pointer: AK_ERR_INVALID_STATE, not a crash
    ak_init(NULL) -> -8, detail 3
    ak_init(NULL, NULL) -> -8
log-bridge                   ok     the host's ak_log_fn receives a line
        [host log, ctx=0x0] a line from the core
    ak_init -> 0; ak_log_test delivered=1, lines=1
log-declined                 ok     AK_INIT_OWN_LOGGING: no line reaches the host
    ak_init(OWN_LOGGING) -> 0; delivered=0, lines=0
    # The host passed a sink AND the flag; the flag wins, because the
    # flag is the host saying it owns the process log.
panic-hook                   ok     a panic IN THE CORE reaches the host's log, then aborts
    WANT: one line through the host sink, then an abort
        [host log, ctx=0x0] panic in ak-core: panicked at /home/user/ArmoniK.Api/ffi/poc/codec/crates/ak-core/src/lib.rs:269:5:
    deliberate panic inside ak-core, from ak_panic_test
